WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.230
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.230 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.870 --> 01:15.070
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.010 --> 01:21.570
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.350 --> 01:24.080
...is often called this...

01:24.150 --> 01:29.880
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:40.300 --> 01:42.160
Naji, estimated to be five years old.

01:42.270 --> 01:45.430
She was brought to our
laboratory a month ago.

01:46.270 --> 01:50.230
It seems like she's not awakened,
but she acts as an antenna.

01:55.810 --> 01:56.710
Naoya!

01:59.150 --> 02:01.740
It's coming. It's the sign
of a large earthquake!

02:05.060 --> 02:07.790
The dreadful evil is
coming out of the ground.

02:10.800 --> 02:12.130
<i>Hope</i>

02:12.130 --> 02:15.930
<i>Hope
Episode 24</i>

02:29.350 --> 02:30.440
Dad!

02:54.010 --> 02:54.900
Watch out!

03:03.850 --> 03:04.840
Are you okay?

03:23.070 --> 03:24.060
Dad!

03:24.140 --> 03:25.030
Are you okay?

03:25.100 --> 03:26.760
Hang in there, Dad!

03:28.210 --> 03:29.230
Damn it...

03:29.340 --> 03:30.970
Hurry, call the ambulance!

03:31.880 --> 03:32.710
Don't move.

03:32.780 --> 03:33.940
W-What are you...

03:54.870 --> 03:55.760
It doesn't hurt...

03:56.930 --> 03:58.490
What did you do to me?

03:58.700 --> 03:59.800
What?

04:02.510 --> 04:03.600
Healing?

04:04.210 --> 04:05.640
I-Is this...

04:06.040 --> 04:08.100
Is this kind of thing really possible?

04:08.250 --> 04:10.440
I just pushed your thoughts a little.

04:10.880 --> 04:13.680
Mr. Namikawa, your desire to heal was strong.

04:17.920 --> 04:19.320
It did come...

04:19.890 --> 04:22.590
But I'm glad. The effect was small.

04:24.100 --> 04:24.720
Yes.

04:28.200 --> 04:30.360
Was that the earthquake you predicted?

04:30.430 --> 04:32.370
Right now, I'm analyzing the data.

04:32.440 --> 04:33.900
Eventually the result will show.

04:34.740 --> 04:35.400
Please.

04:37.140 --> 04:39.200
Thanks. Are you okay?

04:39.480 --> 04:40.380
Yeah.

04:40.880 --> 04:43.400
I might sound sacrilegious, but...

04:43.850 --> 04:46.440
...I'm glad that the earthquake came.

04:46.520 --> 04:47.040
What?

04:47.520 --> 04:48.420
Because...

04:49.150 --> 04:53.090
Now everyone in this town
is going to believe my dad.

04:54.360 --> 04:56.350
Since we came to this town...

04:56.630 --> 04:58.320
...my sister and I...

04:58.430 --> 05:00.290
...and of course my dad too...

05:00.600 --> 05:05.000
...everyone always looked at us
with cold eyes and we suffered a lot.

05:05.900 --> 05:09.530
But your father isn't
doing anything wrong.

05:09.840 --> 05:10.830
Yeah...

05:11.940 --> 05:12.840
But...

05:13.740 --> 05:17.980
...in this society, if someone
expresses an unpopular opinion...

05:18.050 --> 05:21.680
...or does something different,
people treat them coldly.

05:26.990 --> 05:30.690
I don't have a single friend at school.

05:31.330 --> 05:35.100
My sister's fiance
called off the engagement.

05:35.830 --> 05:37.460
I'm sorry, Lena.

05:37.900 --> 05:40.270
I feel bad for you and Hitomi.

05:40.940 --> 05:44.000
But I'm not announcing a lie.

05:44.080 --> 05:45.940
I just want you to understand that.

05:46.580 --> 05:48.010
Yeah, I know.

05:48.580 --> 05:49.670
I believe you.

05:50.380 --> 05:52.980
I'm not holding a
grudge against you, Dad.

05:53.380 --> 05:54.680
I just wish that...

05:54.750 --> 05:59.350
...society would accept listening to a
lot of different opinions and ideas.

06:02.790 --> 06:03.520
This is...

06:03.590 --> 06:04.390
What's wrong!

06:04.460 --> 06:05.720
Look at this.

06:05.930 --> 06:08.060
The one before this
was just a precursor.

06:08.130 --> 06:09.220
Precursor?

06:10.370 --> 06:11.670
What do you mean?

06:11.740 --> 06:13.730
If the earthquake
from before is this wave...

06:13.800 --> 06:16.030
...then the next one
that's coming is this!

06:16.140 --> 06:17.130
It's huge...

06:17.340 --> 06:18.170
When is it coming?

06:18.240 --> 06:19.570
20 hours later...

06:19.680 --> 06:21.800
The margin of error is
plus or minus one hour.

06:22.480 --> 06:23.610
Is it definite?

06:23.680 --> 06:27.640
The cause of earthquakes occurring
can be divided into two large categories.

06:27.790 --> 06:31.650
One is regarding the plates and
the other is caused by active faults.

06:31.890 --> 06:33.380
But the most dreadful thing is...

06:33.460 --> 06:37.390
...when the factors are affected
due to the slight release of seismic energy...

06:37.460 --> 06:40.860
...which leads to an induced explosion
that causes a chain reaction!

06:41.430 --> 06:42.730
Chain reaction?

06:42.800 --> 06:44.600
That's the current situation.

06:46.140 --> 06:49.470
Starting with the plates in this town...

06:49.540 --> 06:52.940
...it will affect the
plates all over Japan.

06:53.340 --> 06:57.180
Eventually it will pull in the
plates in the Sea of Japan...

06:57.250 --> 07:01.550
...and there is a chance it will
damage the whole Pacific Rim.

07:02.020 --> 07:03.450
In that large of a scale...

07:03.890 --> 07:07.290
That is why I am trying
so hard to reach out to the others.

07:08.630 --> 07:11.390
This is a simulation of the
damage from the earthquake...

07:11.460 --> 07:13.790
...according to the calculations
taken from the data we have up to now.

07:13.860 --> 07:15.200
Not just Japan...

07:15.330 --> 07:19.390
...the Philippines, Australia, and
even part of Alaska will be submerged!

07:19.670 --> 07:20.600
Brother...

07:20.870 --> 07:22.030
Look at this.

07:24.210 --> 07:25.180
This is...

07:25.640 --> 07:27.170
Where did you get this?

07:27.710 --> 07:30.370
A five year old girl in Russia drew this.

07:30.450 --> 07:31.680
A five year old girl?

07:32.080 --> 07:34.110
Is there a way to
stop the earthquake?

07:34.190 --> 07:36.050
Of course not!

07:36.390 --> 07:38.880
Right now, predicting earthquakes
is the best we can do.

07:38.960 --> 07:39.920
Brother...

07:39.990 --> 07:41.650
It could be anything. Think!

07:41.960 --> 07:43.860
There has to be... there has
to be something we can do!

07:45.060 --> 07:47.550
There is one thing.
It's not that it doesn't exist...

07:47.630 --> 07:48.260
What is it?

07:48.330 --> 07:50.160
No, that's idiotic! It's impossible!

07:50.230 --> 07:51.500
What type of plan is it?

07:51.570 --> 07:52.660
Tell us!

07:53.370 --> 07:55.860
The earthquake starts by some
kind of seismic energy being released...

07:55.940 --> 07:59.170
...into the plates that pass under this town, but...

07:59.240 --> 08:02.740
...if we can somehow release
that seismic energy somewhere else...

08:02.810 --> 08:05.440
...we might be able to
stop the chain reaction.

08:05.520 --> 08:06.510
Somewhere else?

08:06.580 --> 08:07.550
That's right.

08:07.890 --> 08:12.450
If the seismic energy can be released
at least 10 km away from the plates...

08:12.590 --> 08:13.420
Where is that!

08:13.490 --> 08:14.960
I don't know such a thing!

08:15.360 --> 08:18.450
First of all, there isn't any
possible way to do such a thing.

08:18.730 --> 08:20.490
Lena, I'm going to go
to the municipal building...

08:20.560 --> 08:23.190
...and convince them to call
upon the residents to evacuate.

08:23.270 --> 08:24.360
Dad!

08:32.180 --> 08:33.070
Brother...

08:33.310 --> 08:34.610
That place...

08:34.980 --> 08:37.680
As long as we know
where to release that seismic energy...

08:45.260 --> 08:45.880
Naoya!

08:45.960 --> 08:46.980
Get it together, Naoya!

08:47.060 --> 08:47.890
Mr. Naoya!

09:02.470 --> 09:03.340
Naji?

09:04.210 --> 09:05.300
Naji, is that you?

09:16.750 --> 09:17.690
Naoya!

09:18.220 --> 09:19.480
Are you okay, Naoya?

09:19.590 --> 09:20.680
Mr. Naoya!

09:22.190 --> 09:23.250
Brother...

09:23.690 --> 09:25.320
That drawing that Naji did...

09:29.870 --> 09:31.200
It's here, Brother.

09:31.500 --> 09:33.130
That's where it was.

09:33.600 --> 09:37.170
The spot that Mr. Namikawa
said to release the seismic energy!

09:37.340 --> 09:38.000
What?

09:38.080 --> 09:39.040
Miss Lena...

09:39.340 --> 09:42.400
Is there somewhere in this
town that has a mark like this?

09:43.850 --> 09:44.940
I don't know.

09:45.020 --> 09:46.880
It's my first time
seeing a mark like this.

09:46.950 --> 09:48.780
It has to exist somewhere.

09:48.850 --> 09:50.580
Try to remember...

09:50.820 --> 09:51.650
But...

09:51.860 --> 09:53.550
It was inside a forest.

09:53.890 --> 09:56.790
Somewhere like a
deserted amusement park.

09:56.990 --> 09:58.960
Behind that was a forest and...

10:00.360 --> 10:01.260
Maybe...

10:08.540 --> 10:09.530
Hitomi!

10:09.640 --> 10:10.700
Dad?

10:10.980 --> 10:12.470
Oh, Mr. Namikawa.

10:12.540 --> 10:14.640
We just contacted the
meteorological office and they said...

10:14.710 --> 10:18.050
...there isn't any danger of
it becoming bigger than this.

10:18.120 --> 10:19.100
Thank goodness.

10:19.180 --> 10:21.240
Dad, your prediction was right.

10:21.320 --> 10:22.580
It really helped.

10:22.650 --> 10:24.880
But now the chaos
of the earthquake is over.

10:24.960 --> 10:28.910
Tomorrow, we have a very
important event for this region planned.

10:28.990 --> 10:30.550
That was just a precursor!

10:30.630 --> 10:32.530
Tomorrow, the huge
earthquake is coming!

10:35.030 --> 10:36.330
W-What are you saying?

10:36.400 --> 10:38.770
Hurry and announce an
evacuation to the residents!

10:38.840 --> 10:40.700
Cut it out, Dad!

10:40.770 --> 10:42.100
Y-You...

10:42.170 --> 10:44.610
Hurry up! It's going to be too late!

10:45.480 --> 10:47.240
Don't waste time! Hurry up!

10:47.310 --> 10:48.570
Dad!

10:49.950 --> 10:50.850
Grab him!

10:50.910 --> 10:52.540
Grab that guy!

10:52.950 --> 10:54.110
What are you doing!

10:54.180 --> 10:54.670
Dad!

10:54.750 --> 10:56.150
Stop it! Let go!

10:56.320 --> 10:57.340
Let me go!

10:57.420 --> 10:58.820
Shut him into the conference room!

10:58.890 --> 11:01.150
Call the police and
have them come get him!

11:01.860 --> 11:02.930
You don't care if everyone dies?

11:02.930 --> 11:03.860
You don't care if everyone dies?
Shut up!

11:04.290 --> 11:05.590
Hey, let go!

11:05.900 --> 11:07.560
It's going to be a catastrophe!

11:17.140 --> 11:18.070
It's here.

11:18.880 --> 11:22.240
This used to be an amusement park
that the town was in charge of.

11:22.710 --> 11:25.810
But because people weren't
coming, business became hard...

11:25.880 --> 11:28.780
...so they closed it down three
years ago and left it like this.

11:29.350 --> 11:32.950
If it's here, it's at least 10 km
away from the center of town.

11:34.560 --> 11:35.580
That forest...

11:37.030 --> 11:37.790
Yeah...

11:39.460 --> 11:40.430
Let's go.

11:50.540 --> 11:52.980
Hey, what are you
going to do from here on?

11:53.810 --> 11:54.840
From here on...

11:59.180 --> 12:00.910
We are going to stop the earthquake.

12:00.980 --> 12:01.880
What?

12:04.960 --> 12:06.750
Stop the earthquake...

12:07.660 --> 12:10.630
Am I able to do such a thing?

12:22.340 --> 12:23.270
That's it.

12:23.810 --> 12:26.540
That shrine arch is
really close to that symbol.

12:26.780 --> 12:27.640
What?

12:27.810 --> 12:30.110
Go inside the arch and look up.

12:36.220 --> 12:37.810
Brother, there's no mistake!

12:37.890 --> 12:38.980
It's here!

12:39.420 --> 12:43.880
The message we got
from Naji was to lead us here!

12:45.130 --> 12:48.000
Naoya, Miss Lena, move away.

12:49.130 --> 12:50.070
Miss Lena.

12:59.880 --> 13:01.000
Mr. Naoya...

13:01.410 --> 13:02.470
What is he...

13:21.270 --> 13:22.560
What is he doing?

13:22.830 --> 13:23.860
I don't know...

13:24.230 --> 13:25.860
...what's going to happen.

13:38.120 --> 13:39.340
Mr. Naoto...

13:43.920 --> 13:47.790
Even if you are taken
in by the black flow...

13:47.860 --> 13:51.120
...you are a being
that can never be tainted.

13:51.300 --> 13:53.060
Please absorb everything.

13:53.500 --> 13:55.060
That's your role.

13:56.300 --> 13:57.430
Mr. Naoto...

14:25.960 --> 14:26.450
Brother!

14:34.910 --> 14:35.960
Man...

14:44.350 --> 14:45.540
That was...

14:51.150 --> 14:52.250
Brother!

14:54.860 --> 14:56.050
Come back!

14:56.190 --> 14:57.250
Brother!

15:12.840 --> 15:14.310
Are you okay, Brother?

15:14.710 --> 15:15.770
What about the earthquake?

15:16.210 --> 15:19.080
It's almost the time
Mr. Namikawa was saying.

15:21.490 --> 15:22.350
Brother?

15:30.630 --> 15:34.150
There's nothing else we can do.

15:34.430 --> 15:35.520
I know.

15:39.670 --> 15:41.140
H-He escaped!

15:41.940 --> 15:45.500
Our effort will move
this town and this prefecture.

15:45.580 --> 15:49.380
And eventually the
whole country of Japan!

15:49.510 --> 15:52.280
Without compromising, each and every
one of us should help each other...

15:52.350 --> 15:56.290
...as we change this country
into a beautiful homeland!

15:57.450 --> 15:58.550
Mr. Ikuta!

16:00.220 --> 16:01.050
What!

16:01.120 --> 16:01.890
He escaped?

16:02.260 --> 16:04.060
The roads ahead are grim.

16:04.160 --> 16:07.430
But if we don't fight
against it, nothing will begin!

16:07.500 --> 16:10.130
That is real courage!

16:10.200 --> 16:13.000
I would like to make the slogan of
this town "The Town with Courage."

16:13.600 --> 16:14.970
Who are you?

16:15.040 --> 16:15.940
Hey, you!

16:16.010 --> 16:17.170
Don't get in my way!

16:20.040 --> 16:21.030
Dad!

16:21.410 --> 16:22.670
What are you going to do!

16:24.180 --> 16:25.770
Everyone, please listen!

16:25.850 --> 16:27.210
A large earthquake is coming!

16:27.720 --> 16:28.690
Everyone, run!

16:28.790 --> 16:29.620
Run!

16:30.320 --> 16:31.250
How could he!

16:31.320 --> 16:32.250
Hurry!

16:33.590 --> 16:35.080
Please stop, Dad!

16:47.140 --> 16:48.500
Hurry and call the poli...

16:56.210 --> 16:57.040
It's an earthquake!

16:58.820 --> 16:59.340
Brother!

17:29.750 --> 17:30.510
It stopped?

17:30.580 --> 17:31.510
Dad!

17:34.680 --> 17:35.580
Watch out!

17:43.530 --> 17:44.720
Dad!

17:48.330 --> 17:50.300
I-It was real...

17:55.940 --> 17:57.270
Are you okay?

17:58.410 --> 17:59.570
Dad!

17:59.940 --> 18:02.140
Someone, call an ambulance! Hurry!

18:04.050 --> 18:06.020
Dad! Hang in there!

18:07.980 --> 18:08.920
Please...

18:08.990 --> 18:10.820
Save my dad!

18:32.880 --> 18:33.840
Dad!

18:33.910 --> 18:34.970
Hi...

18:35.610 --> 18:36.810
...tomi...

18:37.410 --> 18:39.250
Le... na...

18:39.480 --> 18:41.510
Don't speak, Mr. Namikawa!

18:41.590 --> 18:42.750
Hitomi...

18:43.290 --> 18:44.340
Lena...

18:45.720 --> 18:46.920
I...

18:48.530 --> 18:50.930
I'm sorry...

18:54.130 --> 18:55.120
Dad!

18:55.200 --> 18:57.360
You can't die! Dad!

19:05.380 --> 19:06.710
No...

19:09.380 --> 19:10.440
Why...

19:11.080 --> 19:14.110
Why does Dad have to die!

19:21.060 --> 19:23.530
The Earth is trying to evolve.

19:24.160 --> 19:28.060
To that end, it's spitting
out the negative energy.

19:45.780 --> 19:48.380
Disaster and war...

19:50.550 --> 19:53.890
But if people realize it...

19:57.930 --> 20:00.400
Even if negative
things don't happen...

20:00.460 --> 20:04.370
...the earth can evolve
in a better direction.

20:17.480 --> 20:21.680
It's been proven that my
dad's research wasn't wrong.

20:22.020 --> 20:24.850
I am going to continue on
with my dad's research.

20:24.920 --> 20:27.150
There are definitely going to
be supporters now on.

20:27.220 --> 20:31.160
And you will be able to
help many more people.

20:32.760 --> 20:33.820
Mr. Naoya...

20:35.630 --> 20:37.290
I'm glad I got to meet you.

20:46.310 --> 20:47.470
Good-bye...

20:49.150 --> 20:51.140
I will come see you again.

21:07.860 --> 21:09.060
Is that so...

21:11.030 --> 21:14.200
She was able to have some hope...

21:14.270 --> 21:16.540
...by interacting with you and Naoya.

21:16.940 --> 21:20.270
That is most likely your roles.

21:20.780 --> 21:24.800
By interacting with you two,
people are able to become positive.

21:25.320 --> 21:26.980
About their own powers...

21:27.180 --> 21:30.180
And this world's future...

21:30.790 --> 21:31.650
Yeah...

22:04.790 --> 22:07.280
Naji drew another drawing, Brother.

22:08.490 --> 22:10.690
It's a very joyful drawing.

22:13.430 --> 22:14.360
Really...

22:31.250 --> 22:34.510
<i>An exact answer is nowhere.</i>

22:34.580 --> 22:37.180
<i>Even if you corner it, it still runs.</i>

22:37.250 --> 22:41.850
<i>It's that kind of repeating all the time.</i>

22:41.930 --> 22:45.160
<i>We hurt each other
and rip each other apart.</i>

22:45.230 --> 22:47.860
<i>We're complaining once again.</i>

22:47.930 --> 22:53.270
<i>When tomorrow comes, just like a lie,
you wear a mask and live on.</i>

22:53.340 --> 22:58.640
<i>I was wishing upon
the night stars...</i>

22:58.710 --> 23:03.980
<i>...for our distance
to become shorter.</i>

23:04.050 --> 23:10.680
<i>But if I try to bluff,
then I'm going to regret it.</i>

23:10.750 --> 23:13.220
<i>Words and feelings are reverse.</i>

23:13.290 --> 23:18.850
<i>Feelings that were asleep,
heart that was asleep, lure it out!</i>

23:18.930 --> 23:24.200
<i>Glamour that was asleep, myself
that was asleep, with your power!</i>

23:24.270 --> 23:29.730
<i>Please look at me quietly with the soul
that you cannot top more than this.</i>

23:29.810 --> 23:34.610
<i>I want you to go wilder inside me.</i>

23:34.680 --> 23:40.140
<i>Eyes that were asleep, emotions
that were asleep, wake them up!</i>

23:40.220 --> 23:45.480
<i>Memories that were asleep, dreams
that were asleep, with your power!</i>

23:45.560 --> 23:51.020
<i>Please melt me with the vision of kindness
that you cannot top more than this.</i>

23:51.090 --> 23:58.190
<i>I want to stay asleep
longer buried inside you.</i>
